 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "File storage on the local disk of the server.",
  "forArchitect": "The simplest Assets adapter and the reason a developer can run the platform with no cloud account. In a scaled-out deployment it is a trap: each instance sees its own disk.",
  "forDeveloper": "Fine for local work and single-instance demos. The moment a second instance appears, move to blob storage — the abstraction means that is a configuration change.",
  "owns": [],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "Local development, CI, or a genuinely single-instance install",
   "You want no external storage dependency"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "Any deployment with more than one instance",
   "Files must survive a container restart",
   "You need a CDN in front of assets"
  ]
